      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re right that a running reload finishes before the job runs again. The requests that arrive meanwhile are also collapsed: request() replaces the pending callback with the latest one and retains the repository-changed flag. Eclipse schedules only one further run of a job when it is scheduled repeatedly while running. So if B, C, and D arrive while A is running then only D will run after A finishes running.\n\n“Batches several requests together” was misleading. I\u0027ve proposed “skip superseded reload requests” for the subject and described that behavior in the commit message.",
